          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For 6–8 weeks: increased low mood, anhedonia, fatigue, poor concentration, and crying most days."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intrusive thoughts of harming baby"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intrusive ego-dystonic images of harming the baby on stairs or smothering the baby. Patient is very distressed, says she would never do it, is scared of the thoughts rather than the baby, and avoids being alone with the baby. No plan or intent to harm the baby."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal ideation"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Passive suicidal ideation: sometimes wishes she would not wake up. No plan or intent; no previous attempts."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
