        "code": {
          "text": "Caffeine intake"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 5–6 cups of instant coffee per day."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental state examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Tired and mildly dishevelled, caring for baby appropriately; cooperative and tearful. Mood described as “really low and anxious”; affect congruent and anxious. Thought process coherent. No psychosis. Orientated, with good insight and judgement."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Risk assessment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Passive suicidal ideation only, with no plan, intent, or access to unusual means. Intrusive infanticidal thoughts are ego-dystonic, with no plan or intent. Good insight, strong attachment to baby, supports from partner and mother, and self-presented. Assessed as low–moderate risk today and suitable for community follow-up."
      }
    },
